### Name
function declarations can only happen at the top level

### Program
func f1() {
  let x = 1
  func f2() {
    print(x)
  }
  f2()
}

f1()

### Failure
[3:7] Parser error (code ##)

 1 | func f1() {
 2 |   let x = 1
 3 |   func f2() {
            ^
An expression was expected here; function expressions should be unnamed (e.g. `let f = func(x) {x + 1}`)
